Q: How to get rid of GTK4: warning: &quot;Gtk-WARNING: GtkGizmo (slider) reported min height -2, but sizes must be &gt;= 0&quot; A: <p>The workaround works, but the `#endif` in the header file must either be commented out or supplemented with the corresponding `#ifndef` and `#define`.</p>
<p>It is also good practice to add a comment to the `#endif` indicating which `#define` it belongs to, as this can save a lot of searching in large source files if an error occurs.</p>
<p>I would write it like this:</p>
<pre><code>#ifndef __LOG_SUPPRESSION_H__
#define __LOG_SUPPRESSION_H__

#include &lt;glib.h&gt;
GLogWriterOutput log_handler(GLogLevelFlags log_level,
                             const GLogField* fields,
                             gsize n_fields,
                             gpointer user_data);
void install_log_suppression();

//define __LOG_SUPPRESSION_H__
#endif 
</code></pre>
